From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] mm: Offer only SIM slots with a SIM, and name them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With two SIM slots oFono's ril plugin names both modems "binder", and the
order of the origins came from the object manager at random. When the empty
slot (an eSIM without a profile) came first, Calls dialed through it and
every call failed with org.ofono.Error.NotAvailable; the dial pad offered
"binder" twice, one of them a slot without a SIM.

Offer a modem as an origin only while it has a usable SIM (state not
"failed"). If no modem has one, offer all of them, so that an emergency call
is still possible. Follow the modems' state: a modem that gets its SIM gets
a new origin, one that loses it loses its origin unless a call is up.
Origins are never moved, since CallsManager would add a moved origin a
second time; they are inserted sorted, with a SIM first, then by device.

Name an oFono SIM slot (device /ril_<n>) "SIM <n+1> · <operator>", with the
own number instead of the operator if known, or "No SIM" when no slot has
one, and keep the name current as the state, number and operator change.
